# Independent Editor path-correction review

The immutable 126-file correction passed 18 independent tests: five exact held-read generation bodies replayed with only import paths changed, eight new path/resource cases, and five new client generation/draft/revision cases. Client bytes are identical to fixed124; reversing the shared path-helper import/extraction reconstructs that earlier server exactly. All old140, fixed124, current126 and original-provenance14 files were authenticated before/after. No production file was edited.

The same 1,096-unit long-path fixture now returns zero matches, reports incomplete results with `editor-path-contract`, and skips the 1,085-unit directory before reading. Actual 1,024-unit ASCII paths search/read/save; 1,025-unit files are skipped and read/save refuse them. Astral path boundaries use UTF-16 units, saved BOM/astral byte revisions and selection coordinates remain linked, and valid leading-space filenames are preserved. A 1,024-unit Unicode path under preview pressure returned 684 matches/2,031,138 bytes with the explicit output limit. Exact 2MiB file and overflow controls passed.

The released bundled ripgrep matched all twelve prepared held-out literal query groups and 267 positions (13 bounded children including version). These reuse seed 0x712ace05 from the preceding collector preparation: that prior collector failed during group zero because it mapped byte offsets against bytes including the leading BOM. This stage fixes only the independent mapper, uses the engine's BOM-stripped decoded stream, and preserves the preceding failed source plus the immutable prior receipt/manifest references. The twelve groups are held out from root's original twenty-group corpus; they are not a new second seed. Direct bundled-engine results are not whole original workbench/editor parity.

The prior original-acquisition proof authenticates the ZIP/publisher hashes and 3,246 extracted files in one fresh pass; its historical signature and before/after ledgers are bound. This review authenticates its 14 source records and current engine bytes, not a second full extracted-tree pass or fresh OS signature check. No native executable or original ZIP was copied.

Acceptance is finite to these source-bound cases. Tests used actual client/server modules in a small element model; no actual browser or HTTP host was used in this independent review. Root's 42 focused tests and earlier seven browser checks remain separately scoped. The search deadline is checked between filesystem awaits, not a hard I/O watchdog. The existing read/save stat/readFile loader and live filesystem-replacement races are not promoted into a stronger allocation/security claim by this correction. No timings, memory measurements, profiling or production integration occurred.

The exact generated fixture census permits a later public subset to omit reproducible workspace payloads while retaining source generators, raw observations and all names/byte hashes. This private freeze includes those files.
